From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:26:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] amdv: route the enhancement layer to a running core1a

Core1a takes VD2 as its EL input only when it starts from off. Under a
kept picture it stays on, so a FEL item after a MEL item enables the
composer EL while VD2 still goes to the VPP, and the picture is black.
---
 drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv_hw.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv_hw.c b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv_hw.c
--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv_hw.c
@@ -0,6 +0,10 @@
 				VSYNC_WR_DV_REG_BITS
 					(AMDV_PATH_CTRL,
 					 0, 0, 1);
+				if (el_enable)
+					VSYNC_WR_DV_REG_BITS
+						(AMDV_PATH_CTRL,
+						 0, 1, 1);
 			} else if (is_aml_tm2_stbmode()) {
 				VSYNC_WR_DV_REG_BITS
 					(AMDV_PATH_CTRL,
